diff --git a/docs/figma/hotbar-notes.md b/docs/figma/hotbar-notes.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..289cc3c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/figma/hotbar-notes.md
@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+# Hotbar: Figma to Roblox notes
+
+Source: `design/figma/hotbar.json` (file "Block Builder - UI", version 2208815566419836712).
+Node `31:100` is the `HUD / Desktop` frame (1920x1080) and node `31:2` is the `Hotbar Slot`
+component set. The export came with no screenshot, so the port was built from the numbers alone.
+
+The frame is 1080 tall, which is the project's reference height, so every Figma pixel is one offset
+in Roblox. The existing `UIScale` (`UI/Screen.luau`) grows the UI on larger screens.
+
+| Figma | Roblox |
+|---|---|
+| Tokens | `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/Theme.luau` |
+| `Hotbar Slot` component set | `UI/HotbarSlot.luau`, with the `UI/HotbarSlot` story |
+| `HUD / Desktop` > `Hotbar` and `Selected Name` | `UI/Hotbar.luau`, with the `UI/Hotbar` story |
+
+## What Roblox can't reproduce exactly
+
+| Design | What the design asks for | What the game uses instead |
+|---|---|---|
+| Selected Name font | Gilroy ExtraBold (800). Roblox doesn't ship Gilroy | Montserrat ExtraBold, the nearest geometric sans Roblox ships. Words come out a little wider than in Figma ("Brick" is 70 px wide there) |
+| Selected Name letter spacing | -0.5 px | None. Roblox text has no letter spacing, so the name is slightly looser than designed |
+| Selected Name stroke | 2 px, outside, black at 60% | A `UIStroke` on the text: 2 px, black, transparency 0.4. Roblox draws text strokes its own way and has no inside/outside setting for text, so the outline's weight may differ a little from Figma's |
+| Hotbar layer opacity 80% | Figma fades the bar and everything in it as one picture | Roblox has no group opacity for plain frames, so the 80% is folded into each layer's own transparency (bar fill, top stroke, slot fills, swatches, key badges, key text, selected outline). Where layers overlap, less of the world shows through than in Figma: a swatch sits on a slot on the bar, so it shows about 1% of the world behind it instead of 20%. A `CanvasGroup` would match exactly, but it re-renders the whole bar every time the selection or hover changes and can look soft when the UI is scaled |
+| Hotbar stroke on the top side only | 2 px inside stroke, white at 12%, on the top edge only, tapering round the 14 px corners | `UIStroke` can't have a weight per side. One 2 px inner `UIStroke` with a `UIGradient` that keeps it fully visible along the top 2 px and fades it out by 14 px down, where the corner curve ends. The ends of the line fade out instead of thinning the way Figma's do |
+| Slot corner smoothing | 12 px radius with 60% corner smoothing (squircle) | A plain 12 px `UICorner`. The corners are circular arcs, so they look slightly tighter than Figma's smoothed ones. A 9-slice image would match, but the slot's fill changes on hover and press, so it stays native |
+
+These parts are exact: fill colors, corner radii, padding and gaps, the 3 px outer gradient outline
+on the selected slot (`UIStroke` with `BorderStrokePosition = Outer` and a `UIGradient`), the
+circular key badge, and the Builder Sans Bold 12 key labels.
+
+## Interpretations and states the design doesn't show
+
+Please review these:
+
+- **Pressed size.** The `Pressed` variant is 60x60 with a 36x36 swatch and the badge 3 px in. In
+  game, each slot keeps a 64x64 cell and the visible slot shrinks to 60x60 around its center, so
+  the other slots don't shift while one is held.
+- **Selected and hovered, selected and pressed.** The design shows `Selected` only at rest. A
+  selected slot under the pointer takes the hover or pressed fill and size and keeps its gradient
+  outline.
+- **Hover on touch.** Hover only happens with a mouse. Touch goes straight from `Default` to
+  `Pressed`.
+- **Gamepad.** The design has no gamepad focus state. Slots still get Roblox's default selection
+  highlight, as before.
+- **See-through blocks.** Window and Ice blocks are see-through in the world, but their swatches
+  are solid, as they were before the reskin.
+- **Show Key.** The component's `Show Key` property is the slot's `ShowKey` prop. The hotbar
+  shows every key, as in the design.
+
+## Behavior that stayed the same
+
+Clicking or tapping a slot still calls `BlockPlacer.setBlockType` through the hotbar's `Select`
+prop, and the number keys 1 to 9 and 0 still select through `BlockPlacer`. The selected slot and
+the name follow the `BlockTypeChanged` signal either way. None of that code changed.
+
+## Layout to check against the design
+
+At a 1920x1080 viewport, in pixels:
+
+| Element | Figma box (x, y, w, h) |
+|---|---|
+| Bar | 594, 972, 732, 84 |
+| Slot n (n from 0) | 604 + 72n, 982, 64, 64 |
+| Swatch in slot n | 616 + 72n, 994, 40, 40 |
+| Key badge in slot n | 608 + 72n, 986, 18, 18 |
+| Selected Name | centered on x 960, y 936, height 28 (width follows the font, see above) |
+
+## Not covered by this design
+
+The frame is desktop only. At scale 1 the bar is 732 px wide (the old one was 630), so on phones
+it takes most of the screen width and can sit under the jump button in the bottom-right corner.
+That was already a problem before the reskin. A phone layout (a smaller slot size or a bar that
+scrolls) needs its own Figma frame.
